  "description": "The **awesome\u2011button** component (type\u202f\u201ccomponent\u201d, version\u202f1.2.3) is a reusable, accessible button built for modern React applications. It lives at\u202fhttps://example.com/awesome-button and its source is hosted in the\u202fexample/awesome-button\u202frepository. Marked as public (private\u202ffalse) and licensed under\u202fMIT, the package is described with the keywords \u201cbutton\u201d, \u201cui\u201d, \u201creact\u201d and \u201caccessible\u201d. Its main entry point is\u202fsrc/index.js, and the build process is driven by two npm scripts:\u202f`build`\u202fruns\u202f`npm run build`\u202fand\u202f`test`\u202fruns\u202f`npm test`. The component ships with a single stylesheet\u202fstyles/main.css, a configuration file at\u202fconfig/component.json, a screenshot image\u202fimages/screenshot.png, and the Roboto font (fonts/roboto.woff2). Additional documentation files include\u202fREADME.md\u202fand\u202fLICENSE. Core dependencies are\u202freact\u202f^17.0.2 and\u202fprop\u2011types\u202f^15.7.2, while a local utility module is provided at\u202fsrc/utils.js, and a remote lodash dependency (^4.17.21) is declared. Custom paths are defined for source, distribution and assets folders (\u201csrc/\u201d, \u201cdist/\u201d, \u201cassets/\u201d), and a Handlebars template\u202ftemplates/button.hbs\u202fis included. A live demonstration can be viewed at\u202fhttps://example.com/awesome-button/demo.  \n\nFor development builds the configuration overrides several settings: the component is treated as private, a\u202f`dev`\u202fscript invokes\u202f`npm run dev`, and ESLint (^7.32.0) is added as a development\u2011only dependency."
}